WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Test 3. This is the IELTS listening test. You will hear a number of different recordings

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.000
and you will have to answer questions on what you hear. There will be time for you to read

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.000
the instructions and questions and you will have a chance to check your work. All the

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:25.000
recordings will be played once only. The test is in four parts. At the end of the test you

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:32.000
will be given 10 minutes to transfer your answers to an answer sheet. Now turn to part

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:41.000
1. Part 1. You will hear a man talking to the

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:48.000
coordinator of a photography club. First you have some time to look at questions 1 to 4.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Now listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 4.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Hello, Wayside Camera Club. Brida speaking. Oh hello, my name's Dan and I'd like to join

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:28.000
your club. That's great, Dan. We have an application form. Would you like to complete

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:35.000
it over the phone? Then you can ask any questions you might have. Oh yes, thanks. OK, so what's

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:47.000
your family name? It's Green, Dan Green. So can I take your email address? Yes, it's dan1068

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:56.000
at market.com. Thanks. And what about your home address? Well, I'm about 10 miles away

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:03.000
from your club in Peacetown. I live in a house there. OK, so what's the house number and

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:22.000
street? It's 52 Marrowfield Street. Is that M-A-R-R-O-W-F-I-E-L-D? That's right. And that's

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:29.000
Peacetown, you said? Uh-huh. So how did you hear about our club? Did you look on the internet?

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:36.000
I usually do that, but this time... well, I was talking to a relative the other day

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:43.000
and he suggested it. Oh, is he a member too? He belongs to another club, but he'd heard

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:50.000
good things about yours. OK. So what do you hope to get from joining? Well, one thing

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:58.000
that really interests me is the competitions that you have. I enjoy entering those. Right.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:05.000
Anything else? Well, I also like to socialise with other photographers. That's great. So

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:12.000
what type of membership would you like? What are the options? It's £30 a year for full

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:20.000
membership, or £20 a year if you're an associate. I think I'll go for the full membership then.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:26.000
That's a good idea because you can't vote in meetings with an associate membership.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:35.000
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 5-10.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:09.000
Now listen and answer questions 5-10.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:19.000
If I could just find out a bit more about you. OK. So you said you wanted to compete.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:27.000
Have you ever won any photography competitions? Not yet, but I have entered three in the past.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:33.000
Oh, that's interesting. So why don't you tell me something about those? Let's start

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:42.000
with the first one. Well, the theme was entitled Domestic Life. I see. So it had to be something

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:48.000
related to the home? Yeah. I chose to take a photo of a family sitting round the dinner

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:57.000
table having a meal. And I didn't win, but I did get some feedback. Oh, what did the

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:05.000
judges say? That it was too busy as a picture. Aha. So it was the composition of the picture

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:12.000
that they criticised? That's right. And once they'd told me that, I could see my mistake.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:19.000
So what was the theme of the second competition? Well, my university was on the coast, and

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:27.000
that area gets a lot of beautiful sunsets. So that was the theme. Oh, sunsets. That's

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:34.000
a great theme. Yes, the instructions were to capture the clouds as well. It couldn't

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:40.000
just be blue sky and a setting sun. Sure, because they give you all those amazing pinks

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:47.000
and purples. Yeah, and I thought I'd done that well, but the feedback was that I should

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:54.000
have waited a bit longer to get the shot. I see. So the timing wasn't right. Yes, I

00:05:54.000 --> 00:06:01.000
took it too soon, basically. And then the third competition I entered was called Animal

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:09.000
Magic. Well, that's a difficult subject. I know. I had to take hundreds of shots. I'm

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:15.000
sure, because animals move all the time. That's what we had to show. There had to be some

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:22.000
movement in the scene. I got a great shot of a fox in the end, but I took it at night

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:30.000
and, well, I suspected that it was a bit dark, which is what I was told. Well, Dan, you seem

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:36.000
to be really keen and we'd be delighted to have you in our club. I'm sure we can help

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.000
with all those areas that you've outlined. Thanks, that's great.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.000
Yeah.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.000
Yeah.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.000
Yeah.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.000
Yeah.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:41.000


